    596  4c04				   BeatFollow
    597  4c04					      subroutine
    598  4c04							; following the keytar: the beat runs on by itself, and each of its beat
    599  4c04							; clocks corrects it. k = steps of this beat already played:
    600  4c04							;   0		the clock is ahead of us: this beat starts now
    601  4c04							;   1 .. spb/2  we're in step: the rest of the beat counts from the clock
    602  4c04							;   more	 the clock is early: skip to the next beat, starting now
    603  4c04							; (After a keytar Start, step 1 waits for the first clock: beatWait.)
    604  4c04		       ad fa c5 	      lda	beatWait
    605  4c07		       f0 11		      beq	.flag
